So once you are berated, you know that's the last one?

Seems a little harsh to set it all the way down at 20%.  This makes an
altar worth about 1.25 artifacts -- pretty rough if you only get one altar
in the entire game, and you get sting on the first offer.  IMO we don't
need to make low-altar games even harder, and this won't do anything to
really limit the number of artifacts in a game with a dozen altars.

This also seems to really unbalance things in favor of classes that can
dip for excalibur, or have guaranteed first artifacts that are useful (W,
V).  Perhaps a better way to do this would be to make the chances of
getting an artifact go like 1/(gifts * artifacts^2) rather than 1/(gifts *
artifacts) -- so that as the number of artifacts goes up, the chances of
getting another go WAY down, but you can still expect to get a few if you
take the time...

